Mattermost's Go code lives in server/ (and server/public, a second module); the repository root
has no go.mod, and dkbuild's godeps fetch runs `go mod download` at the top of the source.
This wrapper module requires the server module, with both modules replaced by their directories,
so that one `go mod download` fills the module cache with everything the server build needs
(server/go.mod pins github.com/mattermost/mattermost/server/public v0.4.3; the build replaces it
with server/public, see the recipe). The wrapper is not used by the build itself.
--- /dev/null
+++ b/go.mod
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+module dkbuild.invalid/mattermost-wrapper
+
+go 1.26
+
+require github.com/mattermost/mattermost/server/v8 v8.0.0
+
+replace github.com/mattermost/mattermost/server/v8 => ./server
+
+replace github.com/mattermost/mattermost/server/public => ./server/public
